# Generated Yul-translation IR lands under rocq/generated/ when the
# regen sweep is run (`bash scripts/ir-rocq-coverage`). Those files
# are gitignored — local working artefacts whose canonical path is
# stable so equivalence proofs can `Require` them by name. They are
# NOT listed below: each generated file emits multiple top-level
# `Definition codes` declarations that collide under coqc when fed
# raw, so they are not part of the main Rocq build.
#
# Once equivalence proofs land under proofs/equivalence/, they are
# added at the bottom of this file as their own tier. Each
# equivalence proof presumes the corresponding generated IR has been
# produced — running scripts/ir-rocq-coverage is a prerequisite for
# that tier. See proofs/equivalence/README.md.

