# --- Equivalence tier ---
# Files under proofs/equivalence/ close the "hand-written sim vs
# generated Yul IR" gap (Audit.v Caveat-5). Each file requires the
# corresponding rocq/generated/<Name>.v to be present, which is
# produced by `scripts/ir-rocq-coverage`. Equivalence proofs are
# added smallest contracts first; ThrottleLib is the proof-of-method
# target whose apparatus (storage projection, leaf lemmas, theorem
# shape) unblocks the rest. See proofs/equivalence/README.md.
#
# Status: Sandbox.v is a working toy; ThrottleLib.v carries the full
# Phase A-F scaffold (Phase C closed, Phases B/D/E/F Admitted under
# R022-family blockers — see WISDOM R022 and the Audit.v Caveat-5
# update for current coverage).
#
# Shallow forms produced by `scripts/shallow-embed-sweep` are listed
# BEFORE the equivalence proofs that Require them. The shallow form
# is the Gallina-monadic translation of the Yul AST — each shallow
# emits one top-level `Module <Name>_<id>` containing all the
# function definitions, so no collision issue (unlike the deep
# `--ir-rocq` outputs which emit multiple top-level definitions).
#
# All five shallow forms compile cleanly with the upstream fixes
# landed on the rocq-of-solidity `integration` branch:
#   - linkersymbol primitive added (commit 2646cf555a) — unblocks
#     every contract calling SafeERC20 / OZ libraries.
#   - YulIf CPS pre-bind in shallow_embed.py (commit c7d737aee0) —
#     defensive layering against M.monadic-vs-Shallow.let_state.
# Regenerate via `bash scripts/shallow-embed-sweep` after pulling
# the upstream changes.
